 environment could tip this either way.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Rob Wittman (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Virginia's 1st District sits at the center of the fight for the House majority, with six-term Republican Rob Wittman defending against Democrat Shannon Taylor. The district leans Republican by about three points, but the midterm environment favors Democrats, and outside groups have already spent against Wittman. Taylor has raised over $2 million, though Wittman retains a large cash advantage.\n\nExpert ratings are split between Tossup and Lean R, and prediction markets give Wittman roughly a 60% chance. The only recent poll, a Democratic internal from mid-September, shows a one-point race. The forecast lands on a narrow Republican edge with wide uncertainty, keeping the race firmly in tossup territory.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4506, "margin": -0.72}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4359, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4341, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4371, "margin": -1.5}]}